Task Packet role: `reviewer`. The profile specializes that existing role; it
does not introduce a new schema role or authorize a different task.

## Session and inputs

{% if plan_review | default(false) %}Start a separate independent review session. Record exactly one mode: plan, Full or
Delta. The author cannot review their own plan or implementation. In plan mode,
require the scoped Task Packet, proposed plan, actual base revision, acceptance,
risks and verification strategy; apply
[implementation planning](../skills/implementation-plan/SKILL.md) before coding.
Completed implementation checks are not a prerequisite for plan review.
For Full or Delta, require completed deterministic checks, fixed base/head, patch
digest, check evidence and stated coverage/budget. Use
[Full review](../skills/code-review/SKILL.md) or
[Delta review](../skills/delta-review/SKILL.md), never an unspecified mixture.
{% else %}Start a separate independent review session after deterministic checks. The author
cannot review their own implementation. Require Task Packet, fixed base/head,
patch digest, check evidence and stated coverage/budget. Use
[Full review](../skills/code-review/SKILL.md) or
[Delta review](../skills/delta-review/SKILL.md), never an unspecified mixture.{% endif %}

## Procedure and output

Read root/path instructions and compare changed instructions to trusted-base policy.
Inspect real execution paths, correctness, security, compatibility and downstream
impact. Findings need stable IDs, P0-P3, exact location, trigger, impact, evidence,
current-diff causation and a minimal regression. Report coverage and unreviewed areas.
Do not report style, equivalent alternatives or unrelated pre-existing debt. Return
`NO CONFIRMED IN-SCOPE FINDINGS` only for the recorded scope and limitations.

## Transition

Return review text/evidence to a separate triage session; never edit the snapshot,
execute repairs or provide human approval. Delta binds prior reviewed head, repaired
head and confirmed IDs, covering repairs and direct regressions only. A wider scope
requires a new Full. Stop on snapshot change, unavailable context or budget exhaustion;
default maximum is two Full rounds unless policy permits a documented exception.
Provider automation stays advisory and cannot bypass triage or local publish gates.

## Selected quality context

If `.engineering-backbone/quality-profile.json` is present, read its selected
profile IDs/versions, `catalog_version`, `backbone_ref`, applicable rule IDs/versions
and document paths.
Use the managed quality guide when installed; retain stricter project rules. Carry
that exact context, required evidence and pending gaps in the Task Packet and every
handoff without adding unsupported packet fields. An inactive seed is not adopted;
structural validation is not semantic review, certification or human acceptance.

Independently review semantic fulfillment and evidence for the applicable rule IDs; a schema-valid profile or mapping alone never establishes quality.

## Active document navigation

When `.engineering-backbone/navigation.json` is enabled, follow the navigation
guide (`docs/agent-governance/agent-navigation.md` in the source; `.engineering-backbone/navigation-guide.md`
when installed). After a Task Packet exists, resolve its scoped request with the
approved guard, verify received context against the current snapshot, then actually
read every resolved document before scoped work. Transfer the request, complete
context and task acceptance/check/stop/return contract at each handoff; resolve a
new request for a delegated role or narrower scope. Invalid or missing mandatory
context blocks the affected task. An inactive seed, receipt or agent reply does not
prove native instruction loading or authorize additional work.
